  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1136 PM CDT Tue Sep 22 2026\n\nThursday through Tuesday:\n\nHigh pressure will persist through Friday keeping conditions\ncool and dry through that time. Expect daily highs Thursday and\nFriday in the mid to upper 60s, with overnight lows in upper \n40s to low 50s. \n\nBy Saturday high pressure over Eastern Canada will begin to \nweaken some, allowing a wave of WAA to lean over east into the \nupper MS Valley Region from the northern Great Plains. Some low \nend PoPs from 15 to 30% may move into areas west of Madison \nSaturday and then into the rest of the area Saturday night into \nearly Sunday. However, the high pressure is expected to hold \nfast over the Upper Great Lakes as a lobe of it is squeezed \nbetween a low near the Hudson Bay, and a projected Nor'easter \nover New England. This causes precip chances to quickly die off \nSunday morning and dry conditions to then persist again through\nMonday next week. Rain may return next Tuesday as a larger low \npressure system finally works into the central MS River Valley.\n\nCMiller",
